From: Aurélien Pommel <aurelien.pommel@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kmsdrm: keep the surfaces when the mode has not changed

Showing a window runs a fullscreen update even when nothing changes (SDL2
returned early there), and KMSDRM_SetWindowFullscreen marks the surfaces
dirty. The first swap then recreates them after the frame was drawn into
the old ones, so that frame is lost. A program that draws once and waits,
like minui-presenter in the Developer pak, stays black. Still so in 3.4.20,
which recreates at the start of the swap but presents the undrawn surface.
---
--- a/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c
+++ b/src/video/kmsdrm/SDL_kmsdrmvideo.c
@@ -1784,6 +1784,15 @@
 
     // If the current window already has surfaces, destroy them before creating other.
     if (windata->gs) {
+        drmModeModeInfo mode;
+
+        // Same mode: keep them. Recreating shows the console and loses this frame.
+        KMSDRM_GetModeToSet(window, &mode);
+        if (SDL_memcmp(&mode, &dispdata->mode, sizeof(mode)) == 0) {
+            windata->egl_surface_dirty = false;
+            return true;
+        }
+
         KMSDRM_DestroySurfaces(_this, window);
     }
 
